diff -ruN gm_orig/docs/telemetry.md gm_mod/docs/telemetry.md
--- gm_orig/docs/telemetry.md	2026-04-15 21:37:10.000000000 +0000
+++ gm_mod/docs/telemetry.md	2026-04-19 21:12:55.170151140 +0000
@@ -27,6 +27,14 @@
 
 The metadata sidecar is the source of truth for channel descriptions and shot context.
 
+The tachometer channels are exposed as:
+- `tach_period_us`: filtered time between accepted tach pulses in microseconds
+- `tach_rpm_inst`: instantaneous RPM derived from `tach_period_us`
+- `tach_rpm_ema`: exponentially filtered RPM for easier visual inspection
+- `tach_pulse_count`: total accepted tach pulse count since the last reset
+- `tach_glitch_rejects`: pulses rejected by ISR deglitching or software plausibility checks
+- `tach_timeout`: becomes `1` when RPM is forced to zero because no recent pulse is available
+
 ## Recommended workflow
 
 1. Run the firmware with serial telemetry enabled.
